      {
        "id": 21170,
        "name": "Christopher",
        "username": "Christopher",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-28T16:19:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just because I’m watching this spiral out of control, and I do hate to rain on everyone’s parade: <span class=\"bbcode-b\">Tachyon and Unity are absolutely NOT romantically involved.</span></p>\n<p>Tachyon had already been married for years by the time she invited Unity to come work for her lab.  They butted heads at first, due to their differing ways of approaching issues and Tachyon’s love for order vs. Unity’s love for “just doing things” and not having a thought-out process.  Eventually, they became good friends, understanding and respecting each other’s differences and working well together, both in the lab and on the battlefield.</p>\n<p>Sorry to be a stick in the mud for your ideas, but I hate seeing so much attention being paid towards a path which will ultimately lead to disappointment.</p>\n<p>In exchange for my nay-saying ways, I give you the name of Tachyon’s wife: Dana Bertrand</p>\n<p>Enjoy!</p>",
